{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent negative bias: model forecasts are systematically too low versus realized prices, especially during uptrends/rallies (often ~+5 to +15 EUR by mid-to-late horizon). Apply an upward level correction when recent momentum is positive.",
    "Underreaction / lag to regime shifts: after a breakout from mid-60s to 70s+, the model continues to project near ~69–72 and fails to follow the new higher trajectory. Use a momentum/regime filter: if last 5–10 days show accelerating gains, shift the whole forecast path upward and steepen the slope.",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: bias increases with forecast horizon (small early, large after ~day 7–10). Implement a horizon ramp adjustment (e.g., add a small uplift early that increases progressively toward the back end).",
    "Trend damping / mean-reversion too strong: forecasts revert toward ~69–71 even when realized continues trending to high-70s/80s. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price is making higher highs and higher lows over the last ~2–3 weeks.",
    "Peak/plateau mis-timing: model often predicts flattening or mild pullback while realized continues rising; treat predicted plateaus during strong momentum as likely continuation—replace flat segments with a continued drift upward based on recent slope."
  ]
}
